# Netlify SPA fallback.
#
# Without this, every path except / returns 404 in production. Not "looks
# broken" — an actual 404 from the CDN, before React ever loads. Refreshing
# any page inside the app, bookmarking /dashboard, or sending anyone a link
# to /pricing or /signup all failed. Only the homepage worked, and only
# because index.html is a real file at the root.
#
# The rule says: if the requested path doesn't match a file on disk, serve
# index.html with a 200 and let the client-side router work out the route.
# The 200 matters — a 301/302 would change the URL, and a 404 status would
# tell crawlers the page doesn't exist even while rendering it.
#
# Real files still win. The prerender step (scripts/prerender.mjs, run by
# `npm run build`) writes dist/<route>/index.html for the marketing routes,
# and Netlify serves those directly because they exist. This only catches
# what's left over — which is every authenticated app route, since those
# can't be prerendered.

# ⚠️ THE OLD DOMAIN MUST 301, NOT SERVE.
#
# eliv8os.com became the primary domain on 27 Aug. Netlify does NOT redirect a
# domain alias to the primary — only the www/apex counterpart of the primary is
# redirected for you. Verified live: leadeos.com returned `HTTP/2 200` with no
# Location header, i.e. it was serving the identical site from the same deploy.
#
# Two domains serving byte-identical pages is duplicate content, and the damage
# lands on the NEW domain — search engines pick one canonical themselves, and
# they have years of history pointing at leadeos.com and days pointing here.
#
# ⭐ This also does the job the domain was kept for: leadeos.com holds every
# indexed page, and `utm_source=chatgpt` is the only channel that has ever
# brought this product a stranger. A 301 passes that to eliv8os.com. It works
# only while the domain is still REGISTERED — letting it lapse drops the link,
# and no rule here can substitute for owning the name.
#
# ⚠️ The `!` is load-bearing: without it Netlify serves the file that exists at
# that path (index.html) instead of redirecting. And these MUST stay above the
# SPA fallback below — first match wins.
http://leadeos.com/*       https://eliv8os.com/:splat   301!
https://leadeos.com/*      https://eliv8os.com/:splat   301!
http://www.leadeos.com/*   https://eliv8os.com/:splat   301!
https://www.leadeos.com/*  https://eliv8os.com/:splat   301!

# ── Unstuck Map — its own domain, same site ────────────────────────────────
#
# ⭐ getunstuckmap.com is a Netlify ALIAS of this site, so it serves the same
# build. The product lives under /wayout, so the bare domain has to land there
# or a visitor gets the Eliv8 OS homepage — a B2B contractor advisor — after
# typing the name of a personal money tool.
#
# ⚠️ A NETLIFY ALIAS SERVES THE SAME CONTENT WITH NO REDIRECT, and only the
# www of the PRIMARY domain is redirected automatically. That is what dropped
# www.leadeos.com off the certificate in August and gave every visitor a
# full-page security warning. So www is handled explicitly here, and the
# hostname must be added in Netlify BEFORE these rules mean anything.
#
# ⚠️ The `!` is load-bearing — without it Netlify serves index.html instead.
# 🔴🔴 CHANGED 26 Sep, AND IT HAD BEEN THE WORST BUG ON THE SITE. This pointed at
# /wayout/start — the six-question DIAGNOSTIC — so everybody who typed the domain
# landed on a form. Daniel, seeing it: "there is nothing interesting or intriguing."
# He was right, and the reason is that THE LANDING PAGE EXISTED THE WHOLE TIME and
# nothing reached it: /wayout/hello carries the proposition, a real sample plan with
# real arithmetic, and the crossed-off list. The product's single most persuasive
# object was one route away and no link pointed at it.
#
# ⚠️ The original reasoning still holds and now applies HERE: /wayout is the intake
# and talks to Supabase, so it cannot be prerendered and a crawler would get the SPA
# shell with Eliv8's meta. /wayout/hello needs no session and IS prerendered
# (scripts/prerender.mjs) — so it is real HTML for a link preview, same as /start
# was, and it actually sells.
http://getunstuckmap.com/          https://getunstuckmap.com/wayout/hello  301!
https://getunstuckmap.com/         https://getunstuckmap.com/wayout/hello  301!
http://www.getunstuckmap.com/*     https://getunstuckmap.com/:splat      301!
https://www.getunstuckmap.com/*    https://getunstuckmap.com/:splat      301!

# ── Unstuck Map's own robots / sitemap / llms.txt ─────────────────────────
#
# 🔴 ONE NETLIFY SITE, TWO DOMAINS, ONE /robots.txt PATH. Without these, a
# crawler on getunstuckmap.com reads Eliv8 OS's robots and sitemap — and would
# index a B2B contractor advisor under a personal money tool's domain. These are
# REWRITES (200), not redirects: the file has to be served AT /robots.txt, not
# at some other URL a crawler will not ask for.
https://getunstuckmap.com/robots.txt    /robots-unstuckmap.txt     200!
https://getunstuckmap.com/sitemap.xml   /sitemap-unstuckmap.xml    200!
https://getunstuckmap.com/llms.txt      /llms-unstuckmap.txt       200!
# 🔴 AND THE FAVICON. It was serving Eliv8's — a B2B contractor advisor's mark
# in the browser tab of a personal money tool, on every page. The most visible
# branding leak left after the name change, and the easiest to miss because
# nobody looks at their own favicon.
https://getunstuckmap.com/favicon.svg   /favicon-unstuckmap.svg    200!
http://getunstuckmap.com/robots.txt     /robots-unstuckmap.txt     200!
http://getunstuckmap.com/sitemap.xml    /sitemap-unstuckmap.xml    200!
http://getunstuckmap.com/llms.txt       /llms-unstuckmap.txt       200!
http://getunstuckmap.com/favicon.svg    /favicon-unstuckmap.svg    200!

# ⚠️ Kill the retired prompt chunks.
#
# src/lib/prompts.js used to be bundled and served, so Solomon's full system
# prompt was fetchable with one unauthenticated request. It has been moved
# server-side and the current build emits no such chunk — but Netlify keeps
